WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.333
Hallucination measurement.

2
00:00:02.633 --> 00:00:06.933
If you can't put a number on fabrication, you can't track it, and you can't fix it.

3
00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:09.800
The pipeline has three steps.

4
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.067
First, extract the atomic claims from each output.

5
00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:22.567
Second, verify every claim against trusted sources, using the retrieved context for RAG, with an LLM or an NLI model as the checker.

6
00:00:22.867 --> 00:00:23.660
Third, count.

7
00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.833
The unsupported fraction is your hallucination rate.

8
00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:30.067
Two things make that number actionable.

9
00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:35.133
Fix the denominator: always the same question set, so runs are comparable.

10
00:00:35.433 --> 00:00:36.817
And keep the failures.

11
00:00:36.817 --> 00:00:41.533
Every unsupported claim is a labeled example of how your system fabricates.

12
00:00:42.733 --> 00:00:44.400
Now you can run experiments.

13
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:51.133
Change one thing, such as the reranker, the prompt, or k, rerun on the same questions, and compare the rate.

14
00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:53.633
Here it is in Python.

15
00:00:53.933 --> 00:00:56.667
We loop over the same fixed questions each time.

16
00:00:56.967 --> 00:00:59.533
We split every answer into claims and count them.

17
00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:04.233
If a claim isn't supported by the context, we count it and log the failure.

18
00:01:04.533 --> 00:01:06.233
The final line prints the rate.

19
00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:08.833
Here's how it plays out.

20
00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:13.333
Baseline on Mission Control: eleven percent of claims are unsupported.

21
00:01:13.633 --> 00:01:20.067
The failure log shows two patterns: invented launch dates, and causal conclusions imported from pretraining.

22
00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:28.633
A prompt line saying state only what the context supports, plus a reranker, brings the rate to three percent on the identical questions.

23
00:01:29.833 --> 00:01:30.607
Let's recap.

24
00:01:30.607 --> 00:01:34.733
Extract claims, verify them, and count the unsupported fraction.

25
00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:37.667
Fix the denominator so runs are comparable.

26
00:01:37.967 --> 00:01:40.433
Keep every failure as a labeled example.

27
00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:47.146
And being able to say you cut the rate from eleven to three percent is a strong sentence for any CV.

28
00:01:47.146 --> 00:01:48.300
Next up: Langfuse.
